[[1,2759598,0,0,0,0,"2015-10-08T23:11:44","ChillyHellion","[M]",[],"<p>Hey there! Rule 2 of <a href=\"/v/gaming\">/v/gaming</a>'s community rules requires that post titles include game names where appropriate. Would you mind reposting this with the name of the game in the title? Something like this would work just fine: </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[Age of Empires] One of my Favorite Childhood Games Hasn't Aged Well</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>We just want to avoid a situation where a user can't identify what game a post is about until they click on the link. Including the game name in the title has the added benefit of drawing interest of users who are interested in the game and might not notice the post otherwise.</p>\n<p>If Voat's site-wide repost filter catches your post, just include a question mark (?) at the end of your URL, like this: </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>http://waywardstrategist.com/2015/10/08/one-of-my-favorite-childhood-real-time-strategy-games-hasnt-aged-well/?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That should let your post through and still end up on the same webpage. Let me know if I can assist you and thank you for posting to <a href=\"/v/gaming\">/v/gaming</a>! </p>"],[2,2760222,2759598,1,0,1,"2015-10-09T00:07:19","waywardstrategy","",[],"<p>Ah sorry Chilly! I didn't know. Yeah, I can repost with the game's name, NBD. This feedback is about 10000000x more clear than reddit, BTW. Thanks!</p>"],[3,2760434,2760222,3,0,3,"2015-10-09T00:25:54","ChillyHellion","",[],"<p>No worries! And I appreciate the feedback; <a href=\"/v/gaming\">/v/gaming</a> has a great community and it doesn't take much on my part to be detailed and respectful in return. Sometimes our modcomments can be rushed if we're in a hurry, but the modteam really appreciates the <a href=\"/v/gaming\">/v/gaming</a> community and just wants to help wherever possible. Thank you for your feedback and for the title correction. I'm going to link <a href=\"https://voat.co/v/gaming/comments/573817\">your new post</a> for anyone who comes across this interaction in the modlog and wants to find it. Thanks for posting and happy gaming! </p>"]]
[[0,573671,0,8,0,8,"2015-10-08T22:55:21","loltidderkcuf","",[],"","Sad Georgia Fans: \"It's like an antidepressant commercial that never gets to the part when they tell you about the drug.\"","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TpSroBuQDpc","RTR"],[1,2760250,0,1,0,1,"2015-10-09T00:09:32","Firevine","",[],"<p>You'd think Georgians would be used to being disappointed by our associated sports teams by now. I sure as shit learned it about 20 years ago.</p>"]]
[[0,573672,0,46,3,43,"2015-10-08T22:56:09","OhBlindOne","",[],"","Judge Shuts Down Hillary's Request to Combine Her Trials","http://www.breitbart.com/big-government/2015/10/08/judge-shuts-hillarys-request-combine-trials-one/","politics"],[1,2759428,0,6,0,6,"2015-10-08T22:57:36","BitchoftheBunch","",[],"<p>Hillary: &quot;I ask...no I DEMAND GODDAMMIT that you combine all my crimes into one mega charge and throw that case out!&quot;</p>"],[2,2759589,2759428,6,0,6,"2015-10-08T23:11:12","VoutGuy","",[],"<p>Further down:\r\nHilarity: Of course they're related! They're all about me!</p>"],[3,2759630,2759589,4,0,4,"2015-10-08T23:14:37","BitchoftheBunch","[e]",[],"<p>LOL this woman should be in a sideshow...with her fucking maniac face a la joker</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://libertyunyielding.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/Hillary-scary-face.jpg\">Why so serious?</a></p>"],[1,2759865,0,8,0,8,"2015-10-08T23:35:53","Super_Cooper","",[],"<p>This is good news, but I would like to see some criminal charges pressed against her as well, considering the fact that she has committed several already.</p>"],[2,2760612,2759865,2,7,-5,"2015-10-09T00:40:09","Kaizervonmaanen","",[],"<p>She is rich, republicans want rich people to be above the law so they don't want to create a precedent where rich people get in trouble for every little illegal thing they do. It might backfire no matter how much they dislike Clinton.</p>"],[3,2763798,2760612,2,0,2,"2015-10-09T05:00:04","Super_Cooper","",[],"<p>To a certain degree, rich people will always be above the law. They have access to the best lawyers and politicians. Look at the way the rich and powerful avoided prosecution for molesting little boys in lefty London. You can't blame that on Republicans. </p>"],[1,2761434,0,1,0,1,"2015-10-09T01:44:59","Kronicals","",[],"<p>How trustworthy is breitbart? Never heard of it until now.</p>"],[2,2761974,2761434,3,0,3,"2015-10-09T02:25:45","ShinyVoater","",[],"<p>Somebody clearly hasn't been lurking. It's pretty popular to post from and fairly right-wing, but I don't recall I've seen any obvious lying, so I'd trust them well enough, especially since they do tell the honest truth in a number of cases where the more mainstream media has spun the subject to hell and gone.</p>"],[3,2762047,2761974,0,0,0,"2015-10-09T02:31:11","Kronicals","",[],"<p>Thanks. Ya no real lurking, just left Reddit because it felt like an echo chamber with a lack of any meaningful discussion. Go to comments thinking I'd find a good discussion... and top comments another dick joke.</p>"],[4,2762230,2762047,2,0,2,"2015-10-09T02:46:32","ShinyVoater","",[],"<p>The comments can be a bit uneven, definitely, but decent discussions don't get shut down left, right and center like they did when I was on reddit(though you'll have to wade through dick jokes <em>anywhere</em> that sorts by score).</p>"],[1,2762908,0,0,0,0,"2015-10-09T03:41:24","ShampocalypseWOW","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1ytCEuuW2_A\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1ytCEuuW2_A</a></p>"]]
